::ENG2_U01_L01_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The school store began selling plain folders after students said decorated folders were too expensive. The manager explained that the new option helped students buy supplies without spending as much money. Question: Which choice best paraphrases the passage?{
=A. The school store added a less expensive folder option after students said decorated folders cost too much.#Correct. This keeps the key idea and important reason from the passage.
~B. The school store stopped selling folders because students refused to buy supplies.#Incorrect. The passage says the store began selling plain folders, not that it stopped selling folders.
~C. Students decorated folders because the school store manager asked them to save money.#Incorrect. This changes the action and adds information that is not in the passage.
~D. The manager sold expensive folders because students wanted more decorations.#Incorrect. This states the opposite of the passage.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: After the hallway became crowded before first period, the principal opened an extra entrance near the gym. Students who had classes on that side of the building could now enter more quickly. Question: What is the most accurate paraphrase?{
~A. The principal closed the gym entrance because students were late to class.#Incorrect. The passage says an extra entrance opened, not closed.
=B. The principal opened another entrance to reduce crowding and help some students get inside faster.#Correct. This accurately restates the problem, action, and result.
~C. Students entered through the gym because first period was moved to a different building.#Incorrect. The passage does not say first period moved.
~D. The hallway became crowded because students wanted to use only one entrance.#Incorrect. The passage does not explain student preference as the cause.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A science club planted native flowers beside the track because those plants need less watering than many decorative flowers. The club hoped the garden would save water and attract butterflies. Question: Which paraphrase is accurate?{
~A. The science club removed flowers from the track because butterflies needed more water.#Incorrect. This reverses the action and confuses the reason.
~B. Native flowers were planted because decorative flowers attract too many butterflies.#Incorrect. The passage does not say decorative flowers attract too many butterflies.
=C. The science club used native flowers near the track because they require less water and may attract butterflies.#Correct. This includes the main action and both reasons from the passage.
~D. The club watered decorative flowers beside the track to keep butterflies away.#Incorrect. This contradicts the passage.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The yearbook staff interviewed students from each grade before choosing a cover design. They wanted the cover to represent the whole school, not only one group of students. Question: What is the main idea?{
~A. The yearbook staff let only one grade design the cover.#Incorrect. The passage says the staff interviewed students from each grade.
~B. The yearbook staff could not choose a cover because students disagreed.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the staff failed to choose a cover.
~C. The yearbook staff canceled interviews because the cover already represented everyone.#Incorrect. The passage says interviews happened before the design choice.
=D. The yearbook staff gathered opinions so the cover would represent the entire school.#Correct. This captures the main idea and purpose of the interviews.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The bus driver reminded students to keep backpacks out of the aisle. She explained that clear aisles help people move safely if the bus stops suddenly. Question: Which choice best paraphrases the passage?{
=A. The bus driver said backpacks should stay out of the aisle so people can move safely.#Correct. This accurately restates the direction and reason.
~B. The bus driver asked students to leave backpacks at school because the bus was too full.#Incorrect. The passage does not say students should leave backpacks at school.
~C. Students moved through the aisle because the bus driver stopped suddenly every day.#Incorrect. The passage gives a safety reason, not a daily event.
~D. The bus driver put backpacks in the aisle so students could reach them quickly.#Incorrect. This states the opposite of the direction.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q06::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: During the food drive, the student council sorted cans by type before boxing them. This made it easier for the pantry workers to place the donations on shelves. Question: Which paraphrase is accurate?{
~A. Pantry workers sorted cans because the student council forgot to box them.#Incorrect. The passage says student council sorted and boxed the cans.
~B. The food drive ended because the pantry workers did not have shelves.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the drive ended or that shelves were missing.
=C. Student council members organized cans before packing them so pantry workers could shelve the donations more easily.#Correct. This keeps the action and reason from the passage.
~D. Students placed cans on shelves because the pantry workers could not accept boxes.#Incorrect. This changes both the action and reason.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q07::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The library added a return bin outside the front door so students could drop off books after school hours. The librarian said the bin would help students return books on time even when the library was closed. Question: What is the most accurate paraphrase?{
~A. The librarian closed the library because students were returning too many books late.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the library closed permanently or because of late books.
=B. The library added an outside bin to help students return books when the library was not open.#Correct. This accurately restates the purpose of the bin.
~C. Students could only return books during school hours because the outside bin was removed.#Incorrect. This contradicts the passage.
~D. Students had to keep library books at home because the front door was locked.#Incorrect. The passage says the bin helped students return books after hours.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q08::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A coach asked runners to record their practice times in a shared chart. By looking at the chart, runners could notice patterns and set realistic goals for the next week. Question: Which choice best paraphrases the passage?{
~A. The coach stopped runners from setting goals because practice times changed each week.#Incorrect. The passage says the chart helped runners set goals.
~B. The shared chart replaced practice because runners only needed to read about exercise.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the chart replaced practice.
~C. Runners wrote goals before practice so they would not need to record times.#Incorrect. This reverses the sequence and purpose.
=D. Runners recorded times so they could compare patterns and choose reasonable goals.#Correct. This keeps the action and purpose of the shared chart.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q09::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The cafeteria switched to reusable trays after noticing how many paper trays were thrown away each week. Workers washed the reusable trays after lunch so they could be used again the next day. Question: Which statement is the best paraphrase?{
=A. The cafeteria changed to reusable trays to reduce waste, and workers cleaned them for future use.#Correct. This accurately restates the change, reason, and process.
~B. The cafeteria used more paper trays because reusable trays were hard to wash.#Incorrect. The passage says the cafeteria switched away from paper trays.
~C. Workers threw away reusable trays each week because paper trays were washed after lunch.#Incorrect. This mixes up the details and contradicts the passage.
~D. Students washed paper trays after lunch so the cafeteria could use them again.#Incorrect. The passage says workers washed reusable trays, not students washing paper trays.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q10::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The drama teacher asked actors to pause briefly after important lines. She explained that a short pause gives the audience time to understand what just happened. Question: What is the main idea?{
~A. The drama teacher told actors to speak without stopping so the play would move faster.#Incorrect. This says the opposite of the passage.
~B. The audience paused the play because the actors forgot important lines.#Incorrect. The passage does not say actors forgot lines or the audience paused anything.
~C. Actors were asked to skip important lines because the audience needed more time.#Incorrect. The passage says actors should pause after important lines, not skip them.
=D. The drama teacher wanted actors to use pauses to help the audience understand important moments.#Correct. This captures the instruction and reason.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q11::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A technology club created short videos explaining how to reset passwords. The videos helped new students solve a common problem without waiting for help from the office. Question: Which paraphrase is most accurate?{
~A. The technology club changed every student's password before school started.#Incorrect. The passage says the club created videos, not that it changed passwords.
=B. The technology club made password-reset videos so new students could fix a common issue more quickly.#Correct. This accurately restates the action and purpose.
~C. New students waited in the office because the technology club would not help them.#Incorrect. The passage says the videos helped students avoid waiting.
~D. The office made videos because the technology club had a password problem.#Incorrect. This confuses who created the videos and why.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q12::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The soccer team practiced corner kicks after losing a close game. The coach believed that improving this skill could help the team create more scoring chances. Question: What is the best paraphrase?{
~A. The soccer team stopped practicing after a close game because corner kicks were too difficult.#Incorrect. The passage says the team practiced corner kicks after the game.
~B. The coach blamed corner kicks for every loss during the season.#Incorrect. The passage mentions one close game and a skill to improve, not blame for every loss.
=C. The team worked on corner kicks because the coach thought that skill could lead to more chances to score.#Correct. This keeps the main idea and the coach's reason.
~D. The team won a close game because corner kicks created fewer scoring chances.#Incorrect. This contradicts the passage.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q13::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: When the art room ran low on supplies, students cleaned brushes carefully and shared paint trays. Their teacher said these habits helped materials last longer. Question: Which statement paraphrases the passage accurately?{
=A. Students used careful cleanup and sharing to make limited art supplies last longer.#Correct. This captures the actions and purpose from the passage.
~B. Students stopped painting because the teacher threw away all the brushes.#Incorrect. The passage says students cleaned brushes and shared trays.
~C. The teacher bought new supplies because students refused to share paint trays.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the teacher bought supplies or that students refused to share.
~D. Paint trays lasted longer because students used more paint each day.#Incorrect. This contradicts the idea of conserving supplies.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q14::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The chess club moved its meetings to the media center because the room had larger tables and fewer interruptions. Members said the new space made it easier to concentrate during matches. Question: What is the most accurate paraphrase?{
~A. The chess club stopped meeting because the media center was too noisy.#Incorrect. The passage says the media center had fewer interruptions.
=B. The chess club changed meeting locations because the media center better supported focused play.#Correct. This restates the move and the reason accurately.
~C. Members moved the media center tables because chess matches interrupted other students.#Incorrect. This changes the action and cause.
~D. The chess club needed smaller tables so members could concentrate on matches.#Incorrect. The passage says the room had larger tables.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q15::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A neighborhood group painted house numbers on curbs so emergency drivers could find addresses more quickly at night. The group used reflective paint to make the numbers easier to see. Question: Which choice best paraphrases the passage?{
~A. A neighborhood group painted curbs to decorate the street for a nighttime event.#Incorrect. The purpose was safety and visibility, not decoration.
~B. Emergency drivers painted house numbers because residents could not see the curbs.#Incorrect. The neighborhood group painted the numbers, not emergency drivers.
=C. Residents painted reflective house numbers on curbs to help emergency drivers locate homes faster at night.#Correct. This includes the action, material, and purpose accurately.
~D. Reflective paint was removed from curbs because it made house numbers hard to see.#Incorrect. The passage says reflective paint made numbers easier to see.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q16::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The school newspaper published a correction after misspelling a student's name in an article. The editor said corrections help readers trust that the newspaper cares about accuracy. Question: What is the main idea?{
~A. The newspaper avoided corrections because readers already trusted every article.#Incorrect. The passage says the newspaper published a correction.
~B. The student's name was removed because the editor did not care about accuracy.#Incorrect. This contradicts the passage.
~C. Readers misspelled the editor's name because the article was inaccurate.#Incorrect. This adds information that is not in the passage.
=D. Publishing a correction showed that the newspaper valued accuracy and reader trust.#Correct. This captures the main idea and reason for the correction.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q17::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The gardening club covered young plants before a cold night. Members knew that the covers could trap a little warmth and protect the leaves from frost. Question: Which paraphrase is accurate?{
=A. Garden club members covered young plants to help keep them warm and protect them from frost.#Correct. This accurately restates the action and reason.
~B. The gardening club removed plants before a cold night because frost had already damaged the leaves.#Incorrect. The passage says members covered the plants before the cold night.
~C. Frost protected the plants because members trapped warmth under the leaves.#Incorrect. Frost is the danger, not the protection.
~D. The gardening club watered plants at night so the covers would become colder.#Incorrect. The passage does not mention watering.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q18::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The music teacher divided a difficult song into short sections. Students practiced one section at a time before trying to play the entire song together. Question: What is the best paraphrase?{
~A. The music teacher replaced the song because students could already play it perfectly.#Incorrect. The passage says the song was difficult and divided for practice.
~B. Students played the entire song first because short sections were too easy.#Incorrect. The passage says students practiced sections before the whole song.
=C. The music teacher made a hard song more manageable by having students practice it in smaller parts.#Correct. This accurately restates the strategy and reason.
~D. Students stopped practicing because the teacher divided the music incorrectly.#Incorrect. The passage does not say practice stopped.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q19::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A student designed a poster reminding classmates to silence phones before assemblies. The poster used large letters so people could read the reminder quickly as they entered. Question: Which statement paraphrases the passage accurately?{
~A. The poster told students to use phones during assemblies because large letters were easy to read.#Incorrect. This contradicts the reminder to silence phones.
=B. The poster reminded students to silence phones and used large print so the message was easy to read.#Correct. This includes the message and design purpose.
~C. Classmates entered the assembly slowly because the poster had too many words.#Incorrect. The passage does not say students entered slowly or that there were too many words.
~D. A student silenced every phone before assemblies because posters were not allowed.#Incorrect. This adds actions not stated in the passage.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q20::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The nurse placed a water station near the field during field day. She wanted students to drink water between events instead of waiting until they felt very thirsty. Question: What is the main idea?{
~A. The nurse removed water from the field because students were too thirsty.#Incorrect. The nurse added a water station.
~B. Students waited for the nurse before they could join field day events.#Incorrect. The passage does not say students waited for the nurse.
~C. The water station was placed inside the classroom because outdoor events were canceled.#Incorrect. The passage says the station was near the field.
=D. The nurse set up water near the field to encourage students to stay hydrated during field day.#Correct. This accurately captures the action and purpose.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q21::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The robotics team tested its machine on carpet and tile because the competition floor could include both surfaces. The team adjusted the wheels after seeing how the robot moved on each one. Question: Which paraphrase is most accurate?{
=A. The team tested the robot on different surfaces and changed the wheels based on how it moved.#Correct. This accurately restates the testing and adjustment process.
~B. The robotics team avoided testing because the competition floor was unknown.#Incorrect. The passage says the team tested on both surfaces.
~C. The competition required students to replace tile with carpet before testing the robot.#Incorrect. The passage does not say students changed the competition floor.
~D. The robot moved perfectly on every surface, so the team did not adjust anything.#Incorrect. The passage says the team adjusted the wheels.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q22::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A teacher asked students to underline sentences that proved their answers. She explained that evidence helps readers see where an idea came from in the text. Question: Which choice best paraphrases the passage?{
~A. Students underlined random sentences because the teacher did not want evidence.#Incorrect. The passage says students underlined sentences that proved their answers.
=B. The teacher had students mark text evidence so their answers could be connected to the passage.#Correct. This accurately restates the direction and reason.
~C. Readers ignored the text because evidence made answers harder to find.#Incorrect. The passage says evidence helps readers see where ideas came from.
~D. The teacher asked students to erase answers that came from the passage.#Incorrect. This contradicts the passage.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q23::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The recycling club weighed paper collected from classrooms each Friday. The weekly totals helped the club see whether its reminders were increasing participation. Question: What is the most accurate paraphrase?{
~A. The recycling club weighed paper once because reminders were no longer needed.#Incorrect. The passage says the club weighed paper each Friday.
~B. Classrooms stopped recycling because the club collected too much paper.#Incorrect. The passage does not say recycling stopped.
=C. The club used weekly paper totals to check whether more people were participating in recycling.#Correct. This keeps the main idea and purpose.
~D. Reminders increased because the club did not collect paper from classrooms.#Incorrect. This contradicts the passage.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q24::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The principal recorded morning announcements so students who arrived late could watch them later. This helped absent or late students receive the same information as everyone else. Question: Which statement is the best paraphrase?{
~A. The principal stopped announcements because late students already knew the information.#Incorrect. The principal recorded announcements, not stopped them.
~B. Students who arrived late made announcements for everyone else to watch.#Incorrect. The principal recorded the announcements.
~C. Morning announcements were recorded because everyone arrived at the same time.#Incorrect. The recording helped students who were absent or late.
=D. Recorded announcements helped absent or late students access the information they missed.#Correct. This accurately restates the action and purpose.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_Q25::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A volunteer group labeled storage boxes in the art closet. Because each label listed the supplies inside, students could find materials without opening every box. Question: What is the main idea?{
~A. Students opened every storage box because the labels were missing.#Incorrect. The passage says labels prevented students from needing to open every box.
=B. Labels helped students locate art supplies more efficiently.#Correct. This captures the main idea of the passage.
~C. Volunteers removed supplies from the art closet because boxes were confusing.#Incorrect. The passage says volunteers labeled boxes, not removed supplies.
~D. The art closet closed because students could not find materials.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the closet closed.
}

